hi my name is presh  salvatika my name is pinuli chai i'm his  mother so this summer is really special  to us because we're going to be opening  our first restaurant at the thai town  marketplace it's called the poke please  and we're going to be sharing two family  recipes with you so the first dish is  going to be our take on a traditional  thai dish called  we used a pork shoshu made with pork  belly we  roll it up into this beautiful meat  parcel so you have like a slab pork you  just roll it up and then you take twine  and you tie off one end and then you  keep moving down tied up the pork belly  until you have it all the way through  you want to make sure that it's tight  otherwise it'll fall apart when it's  boiling so after the pork's all tied up  we just quickly sear it in the pot  so the broth has a bunch of different  components we start off with sake urine  soy sauce and then we add brown sugar  star anise coriander black pepper and  then after that we add crushed shallots  whole garlic and crushed ginger  and we steep it overnight but if it's in  it you're like you're out of time you  can do it like four to six hours once  it's nice and cool we take out the  fridge and we slice it and then we sear  it so you can either use a really hot  pan or a torch if you have one we prefer  using the torch just because it gives it  a nice beautiful char right on the  outside yeah when it's popping it's mean  it's it's it's fried right yeah it's  done yeah it's good next we're going to  teach you how to make the sauce so we  start off with hiki no or bird's eye  chilies we put in an even amount of  garlic fish sauce sugar  and lime juice so you can do this like  in a food processor or blender you're  just going to start off with a bed of  rice you're going to put cork toshu  right on top and then right on top of  the pork you're going to put the  thai  chili lime sauce  and you can top it off with sesame seeds  or green onions or really anything you  want after that you're gonna add your  soft boiled egg and that's how you make  our version of a cow cow  our next dish is a thai lab we have  adapted it and made it so that it tastes  really good with raw fish or sashimi  first off we start off with toasting all  the dry ingredients in a pan the spices  we start off with are  dried thai chilies we also use shallots  lemongrass coriander and garlic once  you've toasted all those ingredients  you're going to want to put them into a  food processor and blend them until  they're smooth you're going to set them  on the side for a little bit take a pan  and you're going to cook thai shrimp  paste you're going to add some oil and  throw in all that stuff that you got  from the blender or the food processor  by the final stage it should be like  almost like a paste today we're going to  be using salmon i personally love salmon  you want to make sure that it's this  nice deep color you don't ever want to  buy fish if you're gonna eat it raw if  it smells fishy so we're cutting it  lengthwise so you're gonna be cutting it  against the grain after that you're  gonna cut into cubes i personally like  kind of big cubes but you can cut them  as small or as big as you want put in a  few spoonfuls of that lab sauce you're  going to mix it in and then you're going  to throw in cilantro mint and we also  put in something called hot pound it's  like a  bamboo leaf but it's smaller it's softer  you are just going to put it over a bed  of rice i personally like topping it off  with fried garlic red onions and then  some more green onions on top and then  we garnish it with some thinly sliced  radishes and that's how you make our lab  pokey  so good super good  [Music]  you

